<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "State natively the requirements worth keeping from a legacy-mining exercise, and remove the mechanism that discovered them. Three requirements survive because they are still required, are declared nowhere else, and can be said entirely in current terms. One of the three was measurably unsatisfied, so satisfying it is part of this work rather than a finding left open." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Measured 2026-09-04. A reachability observation over the tracked tree found 175 production units, 170 reachable from some declared root, five reachable from none: src/semantic/store.ts, query.ts and n3.d.ts, plus two unrelated units. src/semantic imports n3, oxigraph and rdf-validate-shacl -- three production dependencies for a second RDF ingestion stack that nothing imports. The mining graph's own requirement said to unify or retire exactly that second path rather than maintain two truths, so the requirement and its violation were discovered together. The mechanism itself is 5431 lines whose only reachability is its own test, and five of its requirements describe commands that were never registered: usf graph offers execute, integrity and lanes, not inspect, export, import, coverage or inventory." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Local, hermetic and deterministic. It removes implementation and dependencies, states four requirements, and contacts nothing." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
