<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Eighteen of the mining graph's twenty-one requirements are deliberately not carried forward. Six are already stated in current authority and would be duplicates. Twelve describe the mechanism itself -- its inventory, its source-selection contract, its extraction profile, its candidate identity, and five commands that were never registered -- and have no meaning once the mechanism is gone." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "graph/semantic-recovery.nq and graph/foundation.nq are deliberately untouched. Both are pinned in an immutable historical-carrier record with observedCurrentnessDisposition exact-present, and foundation.nq additionally holds a dated disposition derived over all nine declared profiles. Retiring a pinned carrier member is its own declared act, not a side effect of removing an implementation." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:contract:semantic-authority-path:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Removing a second ingestion stack is not a claim that the remaining one is complete. It is a claim that there is one of them, which is what the requirement asks." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
