<urn:usf:requirement:single-semantic-ingestion-path> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Graph-manifest version two import expansion, strict source validation and canonical dataset identity are the only operational path by which semantic authority is ingested. A second ingestion stack is a defect whether or not anything currently calls it, because two implementations of one decision can disagree and the unused one is the one nobody notices diverging." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:requirement:single-semantic-ingestion-path> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "one ingestion implementation; a second is a finding, not a spare." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
<urn:usf:requirement:single-semantic-ingestion-path> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "An unused second stack is not harmless. It carried three production dependencies, and a reader looking for the ingestion path could reasonably have found the wrong one." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-authority-path> .
